*This is the fourth post (of a series of six) on our six month evaluation* This report outlines our key financial metrics. ## Summary  **80,000 Hours is seeking to raise £360,000 over the next year to cover operating expenses for July 2013  June 2015.** This would cover all of 80,000 Hours’ expenses for this year and give 80,000 Hours 12 months of cash reserves, which would be very valuable for improved organizational planning and stability. Raising £245,000 by June 2014 would give us 6 months of cash reserves. This will enable us to carry out our plans to develop and promote our content about which careers make the most difference, as outlined in (/2013/09/team-plan/). **80,000 Hours’ current financial situation**: As of 20 August 2013, 80,000 Hours has about £30,000 of cash on hand, which is about 2 months of reserves. 80,000 hours’ estimated budget for July 2013  June 2014 is £160,000. 80,000 Hours’ estimated budget for July 2014 - June 2015 is £230,000. In the last year, 80,000 Hours raised £100,000, so we would like funds raised this year to increase by £260,000.

