- URL: https://80000hours.org/2013/02/common-mistakes-in-careers-advice-when-should-you-trust-sayings/
- Topics: Career advice &amp; strategy, Career planning, Communicating ideas, Experience with an emerging power, Job satisfaction, Personal fit, Risk, Skills
“Look after the pennies, and the pounds will look after themselves.” Often in careers advice, as in life generally, you will be handed some proverb. But sometimes these sayings aren’t true, how can you know when to trust them? **A common mistake in career choice is to blindly accept common ideas like this without good reason.** You can’t always rely on hard studies being available, you have to rely on your intuitions a lot of the time. One way of using your intuition better that I’ve found effective is to follow this plan: * Reverse the principle and see if the opposite idea makes sense * Tell two stories, one to explain the principle, one to explain the reverse. * Use these stories to find out when to trust the principle.

