“I prefer to give to local organizations.” I've heard this a lot. Imagine a high school student who sits down to study for exams. Her chemistry book is lying closest to her on the desk, so she decides to study chemistry. Her father points out that since she has an A in chemistry and a D in geometry, studying geometry might help her grades more. “But that book is all the way over there in my backpack,” the student points out; “I prefer to study locally.”

